{number: 99}
{title: ‘Tis the Blessed Hour of Prayer}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
’Tis the [F] blessed hour of prayer, when our hearts lowly bend,
And we gather to Jesus, our [C7] Savior and Friend;
If we [F] come to Him in faith, His pro-[Bb] tection to share,
What a [F] balm for the weary! O how [C7] sweet to be [F] there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F] Blessed hour of prayer,
Blessed hour of [C7] prayer:
What a [F] balm for the [Bb] weary!
O how [F] sweet to [C7] be [F] there!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
’Tis the [F] blessed hour of prayer, when the Savior draws near,
With a tender compassion His [C7] children to hear;
When He [F] tells us we may cast at His [Bb] feet every care,
What a [F] balm for the weary, O how [C7] sweet to be [F] there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
’Tis the [F] blessed hour of prayer, when the tempted and tried
To the Savior Who loves them their [C7] sorrow confide;
With a [F] sympathizing heart He re-[Bb] moves every care;
What a [F] balm for the weary! O how [C7] sweet to be [F] there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
At the [F] blessed hour of prayer, trusting Him we believe
That the blessing we’re needing we’ll [C7] surely receive;
In the [F] fullness of this trust we shall [Bb] lose every care;
What a [F] balm for the weary! O how [C7] sweet to be [F] there!
{end_of_verse}
